@baseUrl = http://localhost:5077

### 1. List bikes (paging wrapper, default page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes

### 2. List bikes, page 1 with 2 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes?page=1&pageSize=2

### 3. Get one bike
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/1

### 4. Get a bike that doesn't exist -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/999

### 5. Create a bike -> 201 + Location header
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Kona Dew",
  "type": "City",
  "pricePerHour": 4.50
}

### 6. Create with invalid data -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "",
  "type": "Banana",
  "pricePerHour": 0
}

### 7. Update a bike -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Helkama Jopo",
  "type": "City",
  "pricePerHour": 3.50,
  "inMaintenance": false
}

### 8. Put a bike into maintenance -> 200, status "InMaintenance"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Trek Marlin 7",
  "type": "Mountain",
  "pricePerHour": 5.00,
  "inMaintenance": true
}

### 9. Update a bike that doesn't exist -> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Ghost",
  "type": "City",
  "pricePerHour": 1.00,
  "inMaintenance": false
}

### 10. Soft delete a bike -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/3

### 11. Get the deleted bike -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/3

### 12. Delete it again -> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/3

### 13. List users (for finding user ids)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

  
### 14. Start a rental: user 1 rents bike 1 -> 201, status "Active"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 1,
  "userId": 1
}

### 15. Same user tries a second rental -> 409 UserHasActiveRental
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 4,
  "userId": 1
}

### 16. Another user tries the rented bike -> 409 BikeNotAvailable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 1,
  "userId": 2
}

### 17. Rent a bike in maintenance (bike 5) -> 409 BikeNotAvailable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 5,
  "userId": 2
}

### 18. Rent a bike that doesn't exist -> 404 BikeNotFound
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 999,
  "userId": 2
}

### 19. List all rentals
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals

### 20. Get one rental (use the id from #14's response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/1

### 21. Return the rental -> 200, status "Completed", totalPrice 3.50
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/1/return

### 22. Return it again -> 409 RentalNotActive
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/1/return

### 23. Rental that doesn't exist -> 404 RentalNotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/999

### 24. User 2 rents bike 4 -> 201 (note the rental id in the response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 4,
  "userId": 2
}

### 25. Bike 4 now shows "Rented"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/4

### 26. Try to put the rented bike into maintenance -> 409 BikeRented (S7)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Puky ZL 16",
  "type": "Kids",
  "pricePerHour": 2.00,
  "inMaintenance": true
}

### 27. Try to delete the rented bike -> 409 BikeRented (S8)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/4

### 28. The bike list shows bike 4 as "Rented"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes

### 29. Return the rental (use the id from #24's response) -> 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/2/return

### 30. Bike 4 is "Available" again
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/4